Real trace of `tools/net-probe/run-guest-login.sh` on macOS Intel, no
Xvfb/Wine (native AWT through Cocoa), portable Temurin JDK 25.0.4.1
(tools/jdk/Contents/Home/bin). It reproduces on a Mac the run already
documented in tools/net-probe/README.md (2026-09-10, Linux+Xvfb): same
result, same live server. Trimmed (the repeated lines
`[NATIVE-MOCK] Std.nativeGetMillis()` of the perFrame polling are
collapsed, without removing any line with protocol/state/error content).
No personal data: the nick "FWProbe174" is made up at random by the probe
itself (GuestLoginProbe.main, no argv), it is not a real account.

Command: tools/net-probe/run-guest-login.sh <temporary-workdir>
(builds the mock + the probes in the workdir, copies assets/WorldsPlayer
to a clean CWD, runs GuestLoginProbe gippsland.worlio.com 8265).

