== GuestLoginProbe exit=0 ==

RESULT: state 12 MAINLOOP reached and stable for 12s, lastError=null,
clean close, exit 0 - in substance identical to the result of
2026-09-10 documented in tools/net-probe/README.md (that time on Linux
with Xvfb). It confirms that the real path of the decompiled client
(AutoServer -> AnonRoomServer -> sessionInit -> MAINLOOP) depends neither
on Xvfb nor on anything Linux-specific: on macOS with native AWT (Cocoa)
the same code, against the same live server, gives the same result.
The "a server tried to murder another!" is the same benign warning
already documented (ServerTracker.killServer only prints, it does not
throw - the GuestLoginProbe probe inherits AutoServer without registering
through findOrMake, an artefact of the harness, not of the real client).
